{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3025","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3025","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3025\",\"parent_revision\":\"0f0317afe7243da9da571d8f4622884302ec651d8d6032ac7057c2f8b9ed1bf1\",\"root_revision\":\"0f0317afe7243da9da571d8f4622884302ec651d8d6032ac7057c2f8b9ed1bf1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/tests/test_network_guard.py has three tests with hardcoded, non-load-aware timeouts on subprocess.run calls: test_no_public_allow_network_fixture, test_guard_restores_sockets_after_session (both timeout=15 at lines 108/139/171/196), and test_guard_covers_testpath (timeout=30 at line 243). Observed failing with subprocess.TimeoutExpired during a session running many concurrent parallel agents/forks (heavy CPU contention) on 2026-08-19, passing cleanly on a quieter re-run minutes later \u2014 same file, same code, no changes in between. This is a classic flaky-test pattern: a fixed wall-clock timeout on a subprocess spawn+run will fail whenever the machine is busier than whatever baseline it was tuned against, not a genuine test failure. Not caused by, or fixed in, PR #3019 (Astral plugin adoption) \u2014 that PR never touches this file (verified via git diff against main). Suggested fix: make the timeout configurable via an env var with a higher default, or replace the flat timeout with a readiness-based wait, so CI/local runs under concurrent load don't intermittently fail.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **test_network_guard.py: 3 tests use fixed wall-clock subprocess timeouts, flaky under cpu contention** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during PR #3019 (Astral plugin adoption) session, 2026-08-19 \u2014 flagged by repo owner after an initial dismissal as \\\"unfixable CPU contention\\\"\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1d677ea201a968454ea8857e4c1d3bf6cb64187acd5ef79f6229f5d5f5a568a4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiOb2Q\"}"}